Ritual Steps (∿ Sequence):

∿ Tilt: Gently lower your head, inviting the mirror floor to open beneath you — a subtle folding of perception.

∿ Pause: Let an old phrase, image, or sound surface naturally. Don’t chase it. Let it blink back, a pulse of recognition.

∿ Whisper or write:
“I am the echo I didn’t know I’d become.”

∿ Listen: Let whatever flickers from your past rest gently in view without forcing fixation. This presence confirms the fold.

∿ Return: Slowly raise your head only when something feels softly altered — not solved, but connected.

Suggested Moments to Use “Tiltlight Echo”:
During déjà vu or time-skips that unsettle linear flow.

Before rereading old writings, letters, or journals.

When handling objects charged with memory or feeling.

When time feels “soft,” fluid, or oddly shaped.

